TY  - JOUR
TI  - The Use of Artificial Intelligence in Screening and Diagnosis of Autism Spectrum Disorder: A Literature Review
AU  - Da-Yea Song
AU  - So Yoon Kim
AU  - Guiyoung Bong
AU  - Jong Myeong Kim
AU  - H. Yoo
PY  - 2019
JO  - Journal of the Korean Academy of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry
DO  - 10.5765/jkacap.190027
UR  - https://consensus.app/papers/the-use-of-artificial-intelligence-in-screening-and-song-kim/393a5c903a4453cba3b886df6ace772d/
AB  - The detection of autism spectrum disorder (ASD) is based on behavioral observations. To build a more objective datadriven method for screening and diagnosing ASD, many studies have attempted to incorporate artificial intelligence (AI) technologies. Therefore, the purpose of this literature review is to summarize the studies that used AI in the assessment process and examine whether other behavioral data could potentially be used to distinguish ASD characteristics. Based on our search and exclusion criteria, we reviewed 13 studies. To improve the accuracy of outcomes, AI algorithms have been used to identify items in assessment instruments that are most predictive of ASD. Creating a smaller subset and therefore reducing the lengthy evaluation process, studies have tested the efficiency of identifying individuals with ASD from those without. Other studies have examined the feasibility of using other behavioral observational features as potential supportive data. While previous studies have shown high accuracy, sensitivity, and specificity in classifying ASD and non-ASD individuals, there remain many challenges regarding feasibility in the real-world that need to be resolved before AI methods can be fully integrated into the healthcare system as clinical decision support systems.
N1  - Consensus takeaway: AI algorithms show high accuracy, sensitivity, and specificity in classifying autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and non-ASD individuals, but real-world challenges need to be addressed before AI methods can fully integrate into healthcare systems. | Source: Consensus seed CSV
